    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Young Women"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Where has your love gone,",
          "most beautiful of women?",
          "Which way has he turned?",
          "We will seek him with you."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Woman"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My love has gone down to his garden,",
          "to beds of spice,",
          "to feed in the gardens",
          "and gather lilies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am my love’s and my love is mine;",
          "he feeds among the lilies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Man"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You are as beautiful as Tirzah, my darling,",
          "lovely as Jerusalem,",
          "awe-inspiring as an army with banners."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Turn your eyes away from me,",
          "for they captivate me.",
          "Your hair is like a flock of goats",
          "streaming down from Gilead."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Your teeth are like a flock of ewes",
          "coming up from washing,",
          "each one having a twin,",
          "and not one missing. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Behind your veil,",
          "your brow is like a slice of pomegranate."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There are sixty queens",
          "and eighty concubines",
          "and young women without number."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But my dove, my virtuous one, is unique;",
          "she is the favorite of her mother,",
          "perfect to the one who gave her birth.",
          "Women see her and declare her fortunate;",
          "queens and concubines also, and they sing her praises:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is this who shines like the dawn,",
          "as beautiful as the moon,",
          "bright as the sun,",
          "awe-inspiring as an army with banners?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Woman"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I came down to the walnut grove",
          "to see the blossoms of the valley,",
          "to see if the vines were budding",
          "and the pomegranates blooming."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I didn’t know what was happening to me.",
          "I felt like I was",
          "in a chariot with a nobleman."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Young Women"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Come back, come back, Shulammite!",
          "Come back, come back, that we may look at you!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Man"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How you gaze at the Shulammite,",
          "as you look at the dance of the two camps! ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
